{
  "id": "adjektive-nach-sein",
  "name": "Adjectives: agreement and position",
  "level": "A1",
  "status": "entwurf",
  "variety": "fr-FR",
  "source": "icanspeak French original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-08)",
  "subtitle": "An adjective agrees with its noun: add -e for feminine and -s for plural (un garçon content, une fille contente, des filles contentes). Most adjectives come after the noun (une voiture rouge), but a few short common ones come before it (un petit café, une bonne idée).",
  "briefMarks": ["-e", "-s", "-es", "petit", "grand", "bon", "beau"],
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "article", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "noun" },
      { "text": "adjective", "variant": "verb" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "<span class=\"vp-prep\">un</span> garçon <span class=\"vp-verb\">content</span> · <span class=\"vp-prep\">une</span> fille <span class=\"vp-verb\">contente</span> · <span class=\"vp-prep\">des</span> garçons <span class=\"vp-verb\">contents</span> · <span class=\"vp-prep\">des</span> filles <span class=\"vp-verb\">contentes</span>",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "Most adjectives have four forms: <em>grand, grande, grands, grandes</em>. <em>Mon frère est grand. Ma sœur est grande.</em> In the feminine you hear the last consonant: <em>petit / petite</em>.",
        "tag": "Four forms"
      },
      {
        "html": "Adjectives that already end in <strong>-e</strong> have one form for both genders, and add <strong>-s</strong> in the plural: <em>un pull rouge, une robe rouge, des robes rouges</em>. Same: <em>jeune, facile, sympathique</em>.",
        "tag": "Ending in -e"
      },
      {
        "html": "Some endings change: <strong>-eux → -euse</strong> (<em>heureux, heureuse</em>), <strong>-if → -ive</strong> (<em>actif, active</em>), <strong>-en → -enne</strong> (<em>italien, italienne</em>), <strong>-er → -ère</strong> (<em>cher, chère</em>).",
        "tag": "Changing endings"
      },
      {
        "html": "Three adjectives have a special feminine: <em>beau → belle, nouveau → nouvelle, vieux → vieille</em>. Plural: <em>beaux, nouveaux, vieux</em>.",
        "tag": "beau, nouveau, vieux"
      },
      {
        "html": "Most adjectives come <strong>after</strong> the noun: <em>une voiture rouge, un homme gentil, un restaurant italien</em>. These short common ones come <strong>before</strong>: <em>petit, grand, bon, beau, nouveau, vieux, jeune, joli</em>: <em>un petit café, une bonne idée</em>.",
        "tag": "Position"
      },
      {
        "html": "After <em>être</em>, the adjective still agrees with the subject: <em>La rue est tranquille. Les enfants sont fatigués. Léa est contente.</em>",
        "tag": "After être"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>une maison grand</em> → ✓ <em>une maison grande</em>. ✗ <em>des amis content</em> → ✓ <em>des amis contents</em>. ✗ <em>une rouge voiture</em> → ✓ <em>une voiture rouge</em>. Revise <a href=\"/pluriels\">Plurals</a> and <a href=\"/genre-des-noms\">Nouns and gender</a>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
      "tables": [
        {
          "caption": "The forms of an adjective",
          "head": ["Type", "masc. sing.", "fem. sing.", "masc. pl.", "fem. pl."],
          "rows": [
